const e={id:"docker-what-is-docker-and-why-use-it",title:{en:"What is Docker & Why Use Containers? (Containerization Explained)",hi:"Docker Kya Hai & Containers Kyun Use Karein? (Complete Guide)"},difficulty:"Beginner",readTime:15,sections:[{type:"concept",heading:{en:"1. The 'It Works On My Machine' Problem & Container Isolation",hi:"1. 'Mere Laptop Pe Chal Raha Tha' Problem Aur Containerization"},body:{en:'Every software engineer encounters the painful environment disparity issue:\n> *"It ran flawlessly on my local MacBook with Node v20, but crashed immediately when deployed to the Ubuntu production server!"*\n\n### Why Software Breaks Across Environments:\n- **Operating System Discrepancies**: Different Linux kernel versions, file path separators (`/` vs `\\`), and case sensitivity rules.\n- **Runtime Version Drift**: Developer has Node v20.10; Staging server has Node v18.2; Production has Node v16.\n- **Native Binary Mismatches**: C++ packages like `bcrypt` or `sharp` compiled for Apple Silicon (ARM64) fail on Intel/AMD (x86_64) cloud instances.\n- **Missing System Dependencies**: Missing global packages like `openssl`, `python3`, or `graphicsmagick`.\n\n---\n\n### What is Docker?\n**Docker** is an open-source platform that automates the deployment of applications inside lightweight, portable, self-sufficient software containers.\n- **Container Isolation**: A Docker container packages your code, Node runtime, dependencies, system tools, and environment variables into a single standardized unit.\n- **Immutable Artifacts**: Once a Docker image is built and tested, it runs **identically** on a MacBook, Windows PC, Linux server, AWS ECS, or Kubernetes cluster!',hi:`Har developer ne life mein ye zaroor dekha hai:
> *"Bhai mere laptop par bilkul sahi chal raha tha, production server par jate hi crash ho gaya!"*

### Production Kyun Phat-ta Hai?
- **OS Discrepancy**: Developer Mac par hota hai, server Ubuntu Linux par. File paths aur permissions alag hote hain.
- **Node.js Version Mismatch**: Aapke paas Node v20 hai, server par purana Node v18 hai jisme latest JS syntax support nahi hota.
- **Architecture Difference**: Apple Silicon (M1/M2/M3 ARM64) par compile hua \`bcrypt\` Linux x86 par nahi chalta.
- **Missing Global Libraries**: Server par required system libraries install nahi hoti.

---

### Docker Kya Hai?
**Docker** ek aisa containerization platform hai jo aapke application code, Node.js runtime, dependencies, aur configuration ko ek lightweight, isolated **Container** mein band kar deta hai:
- **Standardized Container**: Ek baar Docker image ban gayi, toh wo duniya ke kisi bhi computer ya cloud server par **100% same** behave karegi.
- **Zero Drift**: "Works on my machine" ka bahana hamesha ke liye khatam ho jata hai!`}},{type:"analogy",heading:{en:"2. Real-World Indian Analogy: Shipping Containers at Mumbai Nhava Sheva (JNPT) Port",hi:"2. Real-World Desi Analogy: Mumbai Nhava Sheva Port Ke Cargo Containers"},body:{en:`### 🚢 The Intermodal Shipping Container Revolution

Before 1956, cargo shipping was chaotic ("Break Bulk Shipping"):
- Workers spent days manually loading 1,000 sacks of spices, 200 boxes of glassware, and 50 barrels of oil individually onto ships.
- Goods got crushed, stolen, spoiled by sea spray, or rejected because the ship's hold had odd dimensions.

### The Invention of the Standardized ISO Container:
In 1956, Malcolm McLean invented the standard **8x8x20 foot steel shipping container**:
1. It does not matter what is inside: electronics, basmati rice, or luxury cars.
2. The cranes at **Mumbai JNPT Port**, the flatbed cargo trucks in Delhi, and the cargo trains in Chennai all use the **exact same standardized twist-locks** and dimensions!

### Docker is the Shipping Container for Software:
- Your application (Express API, React frontend, MongoDB) is the cargo inside.
- Docker provides the standardized steel container.
- Any cloud server (AWS, GCP, DigitalOcean, local laptop) is the crane that loads and runs it effortlessly without caring what programming language is inside!`,hi:`### 🚢 Mumbai JNPT Port Ke Cargo Shipping Containers Ka Example

1950 se pehle jab jahazo par samaan load hota tha:
- Kuli haath se 500 bori masale, 100 kaanch ke bartan aur 50 tel ke peepe jahaz mein load karte the.
- Raste mein samaan toot jata tha, baarish se kharab ho jata tha aur har jahaz ka shape alag hone se load karna mushkil tha.

### Standardized Steel Container Ka Aavishkar:
Standard **Steel Shipping Container** ne duniya badal di:
1. Container ke andar chahe Basmati Chawal ho, iPhone ho ya cement—bahar se har container ka size aur lock mechanism bilkul same hota hai.
2. **Mumbai Nhava Sheva Port** ki crane, truck aur train sab usi standard box ko bina khole utha kar le jate hain.

### Docker Software Ka Shipping Container Hai:
- Aapka code (React, Node.js, Express) container ke andar ka samaan hai.
- Docker use ek standardized steel container bana deta hai.
- Cloud server (AWS, Azure, DigitalOcean) wahi crane hai jo bina dekhe ki andar Python hai ya JavaScript, container ko 1 second mein run kar deta hai!`}},{type:"concept",heading:{en:"3. Virtual Machines (VMs) vs Docker Containers: The Architecture",hi:"3. Virtual Machines vs Docker Containers: Deep Architectural Comparison"},body:{en:`Understanding the architectural boundary between VMs and Containers is the #1 DevOps interview question:

\`\`\`
       [ VIRTUAL MACHINES ]                     [ DOCKER CONTAINERS ]
┌─────────────────────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
│ App 1 (Node)   │  App 2 (Mongo) │       │ App 1 (Node)   │  App 2 (Mongo) │
├────────────────┼────────────────┤       ├────────────────┼────────────────┤
│ Guest OS       │  Guest OS      │       │ Bins / Libs    │  Bins / Libs   │
│ (Ubuntu 2GB)   │  (Alpine 1GB)  │       ├────────────────┴────────────────┤
├────────────────┴────────────────┤       │     Docker Container Engine     │
│       Hypervisor (Type 1/2)     │       ├─────────────────────────────────┤
├─────────────────────────────────┤       │     Host Operating System       │
│     Host Operating System       │       │        (Shared Linux Kernel)    │
├─────────────────────────────────┤       ├─────────────────────────────────┤
│        Physical Server          │       │        Physical Server          │
└─────────────────────────────────┘       └─────────────────────────────────┘
\`\`\`

### Key Architectural Differences:
1. **Shared OS Kernel**:
   - **VMs**: Every virtual machine runs its own full **Guest Operating System** (Ubuntu, CentOS) with separate kernel drivers, consuming 2GB-10GB of disk space and requiring 1-3 minutes to boot.
   - **Containers**: Containers share the **Host Operating System's Linux Kernel**! They isolate processes using Linux **Namespaces** (PID, NET, MNT) and restrict hardware resources using **Control Groups (cgroups)**.
2. **Startup Speed**:
   - VM boot time: **30 to 180 seconds**
   - Container startup time: **Under 1 second (sub-500ms)**
3. **Resource Overhead**:
   - Containers run as native OS processes, incurring **near-zero CPU/RAM virtualization overhead**!`,hi:`VMs aur Containers ke beech ka difference har senior developer interview mein pucha jata hai:

### Mukhya Differences:
1. **Shared Linux Kernel**:
   - **Virtual Machines**: Har VM ke andar apna alag poora Operating System (Ubuntu, Windows) chalta hai. Iski wajah se VM 2GB-5GB RAM aur hard disk le leti hai aur start hone mein 2 minute lagati hai.
   - **Docker Containers**: Containers host computer ka **Linux Kernel share karte hain**! Linux ke **Namespaces** (PID, Network) aur **cgroups** ke zariye processes ko isolate kiya jata hai.
2. **Boot Time**:
   - VM start hone mein 1 se 3 minute lagte hain.
   - Docker container **1 second se kam** mein instantly start ho jata hai!
3. **Resource Efficiency**:
   - Container direct host CPU par native process ki tarah chalta hai, isme koi heavy hypervisor overhead nahi hota.`},code:{language:"dockerfile",filename:"Dockerfile",snippet:`# Production Multi-Stage Dockerfile for Node.js Express API
# Stage 1: Build & Dependencies
FROM node:20-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci --only=production

# Stage 2: Minimal Distroless / Production Runner
FROM node:20-alpine AS runner
WORKDIR /app
# Run as non-root user for enterprise security
USER node
COPY --chown=node:node --from=builder /app/node_modules ./node_modules
COPY --chown=node:node . .

EXPOSE 5000
ENV NODE_ENV=production
CMD ["node", "src/server.js"]`}},{type:"concept",heading:{en:"4. The 5 Core Building Blocks of Docker",hi:"4. Docker Ke 5 Mukhya Pillars (Core Components)"},body:{en:"To master Docker, you must understand these 5 foundational concepts:\n\n1. **Dockerfile**: A plain-text recipe of instructions (`FROM`, `WORKDIR`, `COPY`, `RUN`, `CMD`) describing how to assemble an image.\n2. **Docker Image**: An immutable, read-only template built from ordered filesystem layers (UnionFS). Think of an image as a compiled blueprint class.\n3. **Docker Container**: A runnable, live instance of an image with an ephemeral writable top layer. If an image is a class, a container is an instantiated object!\n4. **Docker Registry (Docker Hub / AWS ECR)**: A cloud repository where pre-built images (like `node:20`, `mongo:7.0`, `redis:7`) are stored and downloaded via `docker pull`.\n5. **Docker Compose**: A declarative YAML tool (`docker-compose.yml`) to orchestrate multi-container full-stack applications (React + Express + MongoDB + Redis) with a single command: `docker compose up`.",hi:"Docker ke ye 5 core concepts clear hone zaroori hain:\n\n1. **Dockerfile**: Ek simple text file jisme step-by-step instructions likhe hote hain ki app image kaise banegi (`FROM node:20`, `COPY`, `RUN npm install`).\n2. **Docker Image**: Read-only immutable template jo Dockerfile se banta hai. Jaise OOP mein Class hoti hai.\n3. **Docker Container**: Image ka live running instance! Jaise Class ka Object hota hai. Container start, stop aur delete ho sakta hai.\n4. **Docker Registry (Docker Hub)**: Jaise code ke liye GitHub hai, waise images store karne ke liye Docker Hub hai (`docker pull mongo`).\n5. **Docker Compose**: Ek single `docker-compose.yml` file se poora MERN stack (React, Express, Mongo, Redis) ek command (`docker compose up`) se chalane ka tool."}},{type:"pitfalls",heading:{en:"5. Production Pitfalls & Security Best Practices",hi:"5. Production Galtiyan Aur Security Best Practices"},body:{en:"### ❌ Critical Mistakes in Production Docker:\n1. **Running Containers as Root**:\n   By default, Docker runs processes as `root`. If an attacker exploits an Express API vulnerability, they gain root privileges on the container! Always add `USER node` before runtime.\n2. **Missing .dockerignore File**:\n   Forgetting a `.dockerignore` copies the local `node_modules` folder, `.env`, and `.git` folders into the image, bloating image sizes to 1.5GB and leaking production secrets!\n3. **Using Huge Base Images**:\n   Using the default `FROM node:20` downloads Ubuntu (~1.1GB). Always use lightweight Alpine Linux: `FROM node:20-alpine` (~130MB)!\n4. **Ignoring Volume Mounts for MongoDB**:\n   Containers are ephemeral. If you run MongoDB in a container without a mounted volume (`-v mongo-data:/data/db`), all database data is permanently lost when the container stops!",hi:"### ❌ Yeh Galtiyan Kabhi Na Karein:\n1. **Root user par container chalana**:\n   Hamesha Dockerfile mein `USER node` use karein taaki hacker ko container ka root access na mile.\n2. **.dockerignore na lagana**:\n   Agar `.dockerignore` nahi banaya, toh aapke local `node_modules` aur `.env` secrets image ke andar chale jayenge aur image 1.5GB ki ho jayegi!\n3. **Badi base image lena**:\n   `FROM node:20` lagane se poora Ubuntu download hota hai (~1GB). Hamesha lightweight `FROM node:20-alpine` (~130MB) use karein.\n4. **MongoDB data volume na lagana**:\n   Container temporary hota hai. Agar MongoDB container bina persistent volume (`-v`) ke restart hua, toh aapka saara database data gayab ho jayega!"}},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"6. Essential Docker CLI Cheat Sheet",hi:"6. Essential Docker Commands Quick Reference"},body:{en:"### 📌 Top Docker Commands for MERN Engineers:\n- `docker build -t my-mern-api .` : Build an image from Dockerfile\n- `docker run -d -p 5000:5000 --name api my-mern-api` : Run container in detached mode on port 5000\n- `docker ps` : List all running containers\n- `docker logs -f <container_id>` : Follow live container console logs\n- `docker exec -it <container_id> sh` : Open an interactive terminal shell inside a running container\n- `docker compose up -d` : Launch entire multi-container MERN stack in background\n- `docker compose down -v` : Stop containers and clean up networks",hi:"### 📌 Zaroori Commands:\n- `docker build -t my-app .` : Dockerfile se naya image banayein\n- `docker run -d -p 5000:5000 my-app` : Background mein port forward karke container chalayein\n- `docker ps` : Currently running containers ki list dekhein\n- `docker logs -f <id>` : Container ke live logs inspect karein\n- `docker exec -it <id> sh` : Container ke andar Linux terminal open karein\n- `docker compose up -d` : Poora MERN stack ek sath launch karein"}}],quiz:[{q:{en:"What fundamental operating system technology allows Docker containers to share the host kernel while maintaining isolated process boundaries?",hi:"Kaun si core Linux technology Docker containers ko host kernel share karne aur process isolation maintain karne ki anumati deti hai?"},question:{en:"What fundamental operating system technology allows Docker containers to share the host kernel while maintaining isolated process boundaries?",hi:"Kaun si core Linux technology Docker containers ko host kernel share karne aur process isolation maintain karne ki anumati deti hai?"},options:[{en:"Linux Namespaces (for isolation) and Control Groups / cgroups (for resource limits)",hi:"Linux Namespaces (isolation ke liye) aur cgroups (CPU/RAM limits ke liye)"},{en:"Type-1 Bare-Metal Hardware Hypervisors",hi:"Type-1 Bare-Metal Hardware Hypervisors"},{en:"Virtual BIOS microcode emulators",hi:"Virtual BIOS microcode emulators"},{en:"Browser local storage sandboxes",hi:"Browser local storage sandboxes"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Docker leverages Linux Namespaces (PID, NET, IPC, MNT, UTS) to create isolated views of system resources and Control Groups (cgroups) to limit CPU and memory usage.",hi:"Linux Namespaces processes ko network, file system aur process IDs isolate karte hain, aur cgroups CPU/RAM quota restrict karte hain."}},{q:{en:"Why do Docker containers start in hundreds of milliseconds compared to Virtual Machines taking several minutes?",hi:"Virtual Machines ke mukable Docker containers milliseconds mein kyun start ho jate hain?"},question:{en:"Why do Docker containers start in hundreds of milliseconds compared to Virtual Machines taking several minutes?",hi:"Virtual Machines ke mukable Docker containers milliseconds mein kyun start ho jate hain?"},options:[{en:"Containers share the already running host kernel and do not boot an entire guest operating system",hi:"Containers host ke pehle se chal rahe kernel ko share karte hain aur unhe poora guest OS boot nahi karna padta"},{en:"Containers disable all CPU register calculations",hi:"Containers CPU calculations disable kar dete hain"},{en:"Containers delete all files before booting",hi:"Containers boot se pehle saari files delete kar dete hain"},{en:"Containers only run when connected to Wi-Fi",hi:"Containers sirf Wi-Fi connected hone par chalte hain"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"A VM must boot a complete guest OS kernel, system services, and drivers. A container is simply an isolated process running directly on the existing host OS kernel.",hi:"VM ko poora naya Operating System boot karna padta hai jabki container host OS par direct process ki tarah chalta hai."}},{q:{en:"What is the relationship between a Docker Image and a Docker Container?",hi:"Docker Image aur Docker Container ke beech kya connection hai?"},question:{en:"What is the relationship between a Docker Image and a Docker Container?",hi:"Docker Image aur Docker Container ke beech kya connection hai?"},options:[{en:"An Image is a read-only blueprint (class); a Container is a runnable live instance (object)",hi:"Image ek read-only blueprint (class) hai; Container uska running instance (object) hai"},{en:"An Image is a text document; a Container is a physical hardware cable",hi:"Image text file hai aur container physical cable hai"},{en:"A Container creates Images only when turned off",hi:"Container sirf band hone par image banata hai"},{en:"They are completely unrelated separate software brands",hi:"Dono bilkul alag alag software hain"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Analogous to Object-Oriented Programming: a Docker Image is the immutable class definition, while a Container is the running, stateful instance of that class.",hi:"Jaise OOP mein Class aur Object hote hain: Image ek blueprint hai aur Container uska live chalne wala instance hai."}},{q:{en:"Why is it considered a major security vulnerability to run production Docker containers as the default root user?",hi:"Production Docker container ko default root user par chalana ek badi security vulnerability kyun hai?"},question:{en:"Why is it considered a major security vulnerability to run production Docker containers as the default root user?",hi:"Production Docker container ko default root user par chalana ek badi security vulnerability kyun hai?"},options:[{en:"If an application exploit occurs, container breakout attacks could grant the attacker root privileges on the underlying host machine",hi:"Agar application hack ho jaye, toh container breakout ke zariye attacker ko host server ka poora root access mil sakta hai"},{en:"Root users cannot connect to the internet",hi:"Root users internet se connect nahi ho sakte"},{en:"Root users automatically invert CSS colors",hi:"Root users colors invert kar dete hain"},{en:"Root containers consume 10x more electricity",hi:"Root containers 10 guna zyada bijli kharch karte hain"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Container root maps to UID 0 by default. A container breakout vulnerability gives the attacker unrestricted root control over the physical host server. Use 'USER node' instead.",hi:"Container root host machine ke root (UID 0) se correspond karta hai. Security ke liye hamesha non-root user (jaise USER node) use karein."}},{q:{en:"What is the primary role of a .dockerignore file in a MERN project?",hi:"MERN project mein .dockerignore file ka mukhya purpose kya hota hai?"},question:{en:"What is the primary role of a .dockerignore file in a MERN project?",hi:"MERN project mein .dockerignore file ka mukhya purpose kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Prevents local node_modules, .env secrets, and .git history from bloating the build context and image layers",hi:"Local node_modules, .env secrets aur .git history ko image ke andar copy hone se rokna"},{en:"Stops Docker from opening port 80",hi:"Docker ko port 80 open karne se rokna"},{en:"Deletes unwanted files from the host desktop automatically",hi:"Desktop se unwanted files delete karna"},{en:"Translates JavaScript code into Python code",hi:"JavaScript ko Python mein convert karna"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:".dockerignore prevents unwanted directories (node_modules, .git, .env) from being sent to the Docker daemon, drastically speeding up builds and preventing secret leaks.",hi:".dockerignore local heavy folders (node_modules) aur secret files (.env) ko image mein jaane se rok kar image size chhota aur safe rakhta hai."}},{q:{en:"Which Dockerfile instruction specifies the base parent image from which the current container build begins?",hi:"Kaun sa Dockerfile instruction base parent image specify karta hai jisse build shuru hota hai?"},question:{en:"Which Dockerfile instruction specifies the base parent image from which the current container build begins?",hi:"Kaun sa Dockerfile instruction base parent image specify karta hai jisse build shuru hota hai?"},options:[{en:"FROM",hi:"FROM"},{en:"START",hi:"START"},{en:"IMPORT",hi:"IMPORT"},{en:"CLONE",hi:"CLONE"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"The 'FROM' instruction sets the base image (e.g., 'FROM node:20-alpine') for all subsequent build instructions.",hi:"'FROM' instruction base image define karta hai jiske upar aapka code aur dependencies build hote hain."}},{q:{en:"What is the key advantage of using Multi-Stage builds in a Dockerfile for a React frontend application?",hi:"React frontend ke Dockerfile mein Multi-Stage build use karne ka sabse bada benefit kya hai?"},question:{en:"What is the key advantage of using Multi-Stage builds in a Dockerfile for a React frontend application?",hi:"React frontend ke Dockerfile mein Multi-Stage build use karne ka sabse bada benefit kya hai?"},options:[{en:"Compiles React in Node.js, then copies only the static /dist HTML/CSS/JS into a tiny Nginx image (~25MB), leaving all dev dependencies behind",hi:"React ko Node mein compile karta hai, fir sirf static HTML/JS ko tiny Nginx image (~25MB) mein copy karta hai"},{en:"Multiplies browser animations by 10x",hi:"Browser animations ko 10 guna fast karna"},{en:"Eliminates the need for HTML and CSS files completely",hi:"HTML aur CSS ki zaroorat khatam karna"},{en:"Allows users to run React on microwave ovens",hi:"React ko kisi bhi device par chalana"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Multi-stage builds decouple the heavy build environment (Node + npm packages ~1GB) from the lightweight runtime (Nginx serving static assets ~25MB), yielding tiny, secure images.",hi:"Multi-stage builds se heavy Node compiler chhoot jata hai aur production image mein sirf static dist files aur lightweight Nginx rehta hai (~25MB)."}},{q:{en:"Which Docker command flag maps host machine port 3000 to container port 5000?",hi:"Host machine ke port 3000 ko container ke port 5000 par map karne ke liye kaun sa flag use hota hai?"},question:{en:"Which Docker command flag maps host machine port 3000 to container port 5000?",hi:"Host machine ke port 3000 ko container ke port 5000 par map karne ke liye kaun sa flag use hota hai?"},options:[{en:"-p 3000:5000",hi:"-p 3000:5000"},{en:"--link 3000-to-5000",hi:"--link 3000-to-5000"},{en:"-port 5000->3000",hi:"-port 5000->3000"},{en:"-route 3000=5000",hi:"-route 3000=5000"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"The syntax for the publish flag is '-p <host_port>:<container_port>'. Hence '-p 3000:5000' exposes container port 5000 on host port 3000.",hi:"Syntax '-p <host_port>:<container_port>' hota hai. Yani bahar ka port 3000 container ke andar ke port 5000 se connect hoga."}},{q:{en:"What happens to data stored inside a container's writable layer when that container is removed with 'docker rm'?",hi:"Jab container ko 'docker rm' se delete kiya jata hai, toh uske writable layer ka data kahan jata hai?"},question:{en:"What happens to data stored inside a container's writable layer when that container is removed with 'docker rm'?",hi:"Jab container ko 'docker rm' se delete kiya jata hai, toh uske writable layer ka data kahan jata hai?"},options:[{en:"The writable layer is destroyed and all unmounted data is permanently deleted (ephemeral lifecycle)",hi:"Writable layer destroy ho jata hai aur unmounted data permanently delete ho jata hai"},{en:"Docker automatically uploads all data to Google Drive",hi:"Docker sara data Google Drive par upload kar deta hai"},{en:"Data is converted into an executable PDF on the desktop",hi:"Data PDF file mein convert ho jata hai"},{en:"Data remains locked in CPU cache forever",hi:"Data CPU cache mein hamesha lock rehta hai"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Containers are stateless and ephemeral by default. To persist state across container deletions, you must use Docker Volumes or Bind Mounts.",hi:"Containers ephemeral hote hain. Persistent data (jaise database files) ke liye hamesha Docker Named Volumes use karna mandatory hota hai."}},{q:{en:"What mechanism should be used in Docker Compose to ensure MongoDB database records survive container restarts and updates?",hi:"Docker Compose mein MongoDB ka data container restart hone ke baad bhi safe rakhne ke liye kya use karna chahiye?"},question:{en:"What mechanism should be used in Docker Compose to ensure MongoDB database records survive container restarts and updates?",hi:"Docker Compose mein MongoDB ka data container restart hone ke baad bhi safe rakhne ke liye kya use karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Named Docker Volumes (e.g., mongo-data:/data/db)",hi:"Named Docker Volumes (e.g., mongo-data:/data/db)"},{en:"Copying files to RAM every 5 minutes",hi:"RAM mein copy karna"},{en:"Running Docker in Debug mode",hi:"Debug mode mein chalana"},{en:"Disabling container termination commands",hi:"Termination commands band karna"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Named Volumes persist independently on the host filesystem and remain intact even when containers are stopped, removed, or recreated.",hi:"Docker Named Volumes host system ke managed area mein data store karte hain jo container delete hone par bhi safe rehta hai."}},{q:{en:"How do separate containers in the same user-defined Docker bridge network discover and communicate with each other?",hi:"Ek hi user-defined Docker bridge network mein alag-alag containers aapas mein kaise communicate karte hain?"},question:{en:"How do separate containers in the same user-defined Docker bridge network discover and communicate with each other?",hi:"Ek hi user-defined Docker bridge network mein alag-alag containers aapas mein kaise communicate karte hain?"},options:[{en:"Via Docker's embedded DNS server using container/service names (e.g., mongodb://mongo:27017)",hi:"Docker ke embedded DNS ke zariye service names use karke (e.g., mongodb://mongo:27017)"},{en:"By pinging public google.com servers continuously",hi:"Google servers ko continuously ping karke"},{en:"Through audio morse code over sound cards",hi:"Sound card se audio signals bhej kar"},{en:"By sharing the exact same MAC address",hi:"Same MAC address share karke"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"User-defined bridge networks provide automatic DNS resolution between containers. Express can connect to MongoDB simply using the service name 'mongo' instead of dynamic IP addresses.",hi:"Docker bridge network automatically container name ko IP address mein resolve kar deta hai, isiliye hardcoded IP ke badle service name 'mongo' use hota hai."}},{q:{en:"What is the difference between the 'RUN' instruction and the 'CMD' instruction in a Dockerfile?",hi:"Dockerfile mein 'RUN' aur 'CMD' instructions ke beech kya fark hota hai?"},question:{en:"What is the difference between the 'RUN' instruction and the 'CMD' instruction in a Dockerfile?",hi:"Dockerfile mein 'RUN' aur 'CMD' instructions ke beech kya fark hota hai?"},options:[{en:"'RUN' executes during image build time to install software; 'CMD' defines the default command executed when the container starts",hi:"'RUN' image build time par software install karta hai; 'CMD' container start hone par run hota hai"},{en:"'RUN' is for Windows; 'CMD' is for Linux",hi:"'RUN' Windows ke liye hai aur 'CMD' Linux ke liye"},{en:"'RUN' deletes files; 'CMD' creates folders",hi:"'RUN' delete karta hai aur 'CMD' folder banata hai"},{en:"There is no difference, both are strictly interchangeable",hi:"Dono mein koi difference nahi hai"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:`'RUN' commits new layers during the image build step (e.g., 'RUN npm install'). 'CMD' specifies the entry command executed when a container is spawned from that image (e.g., 'CMD ["node", "server.js"]').`,hi:"'RUN' build time par chalta hai (jaise npm install) aur naya layer banata hai. 'CMD' container run hote waqt execute hota hai."}},{q:{en:"Which Docker CLI command allows you to open an interactive bash or sh shell inside an already running container?",hi:"Pehle se chal rahe running container ke andar interactive terminal kholne ke liye kaun sa command use hota hai?"},question:{en:"Which Docker CLI command allows you to open an interactive bash or sh shell inside an already running container?",hi:"Pehle se chal rahe running container ke andar interactive terminal kholne ke liye kaun sa command use hota hai?"},options:[{en:"docker exec -it <container_id> sh",hi:"docker exec -it <container_id> sh"},{en:"docker open --window <container_id>",hi:"docker open --window <container_id>"},{en:"docker connect -screen <container_id>",hi:"docker connect -screen <container_id>"},{en:"docker ssh root@container",hi:"docker ssh root@container"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"'docker exec -it <id> sh' executes a command inside a running container with interactive (-i) and pseudo-TTY (-t) flags enabled.",hi:"'docker exec -it <id> sh' interactive terminal allocate karke running container ke file system mein shell open kar deta hai."}},{q:{en:"Why should you prefer 'npm ci' over 'npm install' inside a production Dockerfile?",hi:"Production Dockerfile ke andar 'npm install' ke mukable 'npm ci' kyun prefer kiya jata hai?"},question:{en:"Why should you prefer 'npm ci' over 'npm install' inside a production Dockerfile?",hi:"Production Dockerfile ke andar 'npm install' ke mukable 'npm ci' kyun prefer kiya jata hai?"},options:[{en:"'npm ci' strictly respects package-lock.json, deletes existing node_modules, and ensures 100% deterministic, faster builds",hi:"'npm ci' strictly package-lock.json follow karta hai aur fast, reproducible deterministic install ensure karta hai"},{en:"'npm ci' downloads files via satellite directly",hi:"'npm ci' satellite se direct download karta hai"},{en:"'npm install' is forbidden by European laws",hi:"'npm install' law ke khilaf hai"},{en:"'npm ci' deletes all JavaScript syntax errors",hi:"'npm ci' code ke syntax errors delete kar deta hai"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"'npm ci' (Clean Install) installs exact versions from package-lock.json without modifying it, preventing unexpected dependency drift across environments.",hi:"'npm ci' package-lock.json ke exact versions ko strictly install karta hai aur fast reproducible build deta hai."}},{q:{en:"What is Docker Layer Caching and how can it drastically speed up 'docker build' times?",hi:"Docker Layer Caching kya hai aur yeh 'docker build' time ko kaise dramatically fast karta hai?"},question:{en:"What is Docker Layer Caching and how can it drastically speed up 'docker build' times?",hi:"Docker Layer Caching kya hai aur yeh 'docker build' time ko kaise dramatically fast karta hai?"},options:[{en:"Docker reuses cached layers from previous builds if the instructions and copied files haven't changed (e.g., copying package.json before source code)",hi:"Agar files change nahi hui hain toh Docker pichle build ke layers reuse kar leta hai (jaise pehle package.json copy karna)"},{en:"By skipping compiler safety checks entirely",hi:"Compiler checks ko skip karke"},{en:"By compressing source files into ZIP archives before compiling",hi:"Source files ko zip mein compress karke"},{en:"By turning off CPU coolers during build",hi:"CPU cooling band karke"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"By copying package.json and running 'npm ci' BEFORE copying the rest of your source code, Docker only re-runs npm install when dependencies change, not on every code edit.",hi:"Pehle package.json copy karke npm ci chalane se dependencies cache ho jati hain, aur code change hone par npm dobara install nahi hota."}},{q:{en:"Which command stops and removes all containers, networks, and volumes defined in a docker-compose.yml file?",hi:"docker-compose.yml mein defined containers, networks aur volumes ko stop aur clean karne ke liye kaun sa command use hota hai?"},question:{en:"Which command stops and removes all containers, networks, and volumes defined in a docker-compose.yml file?",hi:"docker-compose.yml mein defined containers, networks aur volumes ko stop aur clean karne ke liye kaun sa command use hota hai?"},options:[{en:"docker compose down -v",hi:"docker compose down -v"},{en:"docker compose destroy --force-all",hi:"docker compose destroy --force-all"},{en:"docker kill compose",hi:"docker kill compose"},{en:"docker compose pause",hi:"docker compose pause"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"'docker compose down' stops and removes containers and networks. The '-v' (or '--volumes') flag also removes named volumes defined in the compose file.",hi:"'docker compose down -v' containers aur networks ke sath-sath named volumes ko bhi clean kar deta hai."}},{q:{en:"What is the purpose of Docker Health Checks defined via the 'HEALTHCHECK' instruction in a Dockerfile?",hi:"Dockerfile mein 'HEALTHCHECK' instruction ka kya purpose hota hai?"},question:{en:"What is the purpose of Docker Health Checks defined via the 'HEALTHCHECK' instruction in a Dockerfile?",hi:"Dockerfile mein 'HEALTHCHECK' instruction ka kya purpose hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Periodically probes an internal endpoint (e.g., curl -f http://localhost:5000/health) to tell Docker if the app is actually alive and ready to receive traffic",hi:"Periodically app ke health endpoint ko test karta hai taaki pata chal sake ki app sach mein traffic lene ke liye ready hai ya nahi"},{en:"Checks the battery health of the server hardware",hi:"Server battery check karna"},{en:"Scans developer keystrokes for typing errors",hi:"Typing mistakes check karna"},{en:"Sends an email to the doctor every 6 hours",hi:"Doctor ko email bhejna"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"A process may be running while being completely locked or unresponsive. HEALTHCHECK commands verify application readiness, allowing orchestrators (Docker Swarm/K8s) to restart unhealthy containers.",hi:"Process chalne ke bavajood app hang ho sakti hai. HEALTHCHECK verify karta hai ki app responsive hai ya nahi, aur orchestrator ko unhealthy container restart karne deta hai."}},{q:{en:"Why is Alpine Linux (e.g., node:20-alpine) widely preferred for production container images over Ubuntu/Debian base images?",hi:"Production container images ke liye Ubuntu ke bajaye Alpine Linux (jaise node:20-alpine) kyun preferred hai?"},question:{en:"Why is Alpine Linux (e.g., node:20-alpine) widely preferred for production container images over Ubuntu/Debian base images?",hi:"Production container images ke liye Ubuntu ke bajaye Alpine Linux (jaise node:20-alpine) kyun preferred hai?"},options:[{en:"Ultra-small footprint (~5MB base OS), lightning-fast download/deployment speeds, and a significantly smaller security attack surface",hi:"Bohot chhota size (~5MB), super-fast download/deploy speed aur kam vulnerabilities"},{en:"Alpine Linux has built-in artificial intelligence models",hi:"Alpine mein AI built-in hoti hai"},{en:"Alpine Linux only runs in Switzerland",hi:"Alpine sirf Switzerland mein chalta hai"},{en:"Ubuntu is blocked by cloud providers",hi:"Ubuntu cloud providers par blocked hai"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Alpine Linux is built on musl libc and busybox, resulting in a 5MB base OS. Smaller images deploy faster across CI/CD pipelines and contain fewer extraneous packages that could harbor vulnerabilities.",hi:"Alpine Linux lightweight hota hai (~5MB). Chhote images deploy karne mein fast hote hain aur unme unnecessary packages na hone se security attack surface kam hota hai."}},{q:{en:"In a MERN stack docker-compose.yml file, what does the 'depends_on' attribute configure?",hi:"MERN docker-compose.yml file mein 'depends_on' attribute kya configure karta hai?"},question:{en:"In a MERN stack docker-compose.yml file, what does the 'depends_on' attribute configure?",hi:"MERN docker-compose.yml file mein 'depends_on' attribute kya configure karta hai?"},options:[{en:"Controls startup order, ensuring MongoDB starts before Express API, and Express API starts before React frontend",hi:"Container startup order control karta hai, jaise Express se pehle MongoDB start ho"},{en:"Downloads extra RAM from cloud servers",hi:"Extra RAM download karna"},{en:"Merges two separate GitHub repositories into one",hi:"Do repos ko ek mein merge karna"},{en:"Limits internet bandwidth to 10kbps",hi:"Internet bandwidth limit karna"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"'depends_on' dictates the startup order of dependent services, ensuring the database container is initialized before the API container attempts to connect.",hi:"'depends_on' services ka startup order define karta hai taaki database pehle initialize ho aur backend connection error na de."}},{q:{en:"What command removes all unused, stopped containers, dangling images, and build caches in one safe sweep?",hi:"Saare stopped containers, unused images aur build cache ko ek sath clean karne ke liye kaun sa command use hota hai?"},question:{en:"What command removes all unused, stopped containers, dangling images, and build caches in one safe sweep?",hi:"Saare stopped containers, unused images aur build cache ko ek sath clean karne ke liye kaun sa command use hota hai?"},options:[{en:"docker system prune",hi:"docker system prune"},{en:"docker format disk",hi:"docker format disk"},{en:"docker erase all",hi:"docker erase all"},{en:"rm -rf /docker",hi:"rm -rf /docker"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"'docker system prune' cleans stopped containers, unused networks, and dangling images. Adding '--volumes' also cleans unused volumes.",hi:"'docker system prune' unused containers, dangling images aur build cache ko delete karke disk space free karta hai."}},{q:{en:"In production Kubernetes or Docker Swarm, why are containers configured with restart policies like 'restart: always' or 'restart: unless-stopped'?",hi:"Production mein containers par 'restart: always' policy kyun lagayi jaati hai?"},question:{en:"In production Kubernetes or Docker Swarm, why are containers configured with restart policies like 'restart: always' or 'restart: unless-stopped'?",hi:"Production mein containers par 'restart: always' policy kyun lagayi jaati hai?"},options:[{en:"Ensures that if an uncaught exception or host server reboot occurs, the container daemon automatically revives the service without manual intervention",hi:"Server reboot ya process crash hone par container ko automatically bina manual intervention ke restart kar deta hai"},{en:"Reboots the container every 30 seconds to refresh RAM",hi:"Har 30 second par container reboot karna"},{en:"Prevents code changes from being saved",hi:"Code changes save hone se rokna"},{en:"Forces all database queries to re-execute 5 times",hi:"Queries ko 5 baar re-run karna"}],answerIndex:0,correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Restart policies guarantee high availability by automatically restarting crashed processes and ensuring services come back up when the physical host system restarts.",hi:"'restart: always' high availability guarantee karta hai; agar server crash ho ya reboot ho, container bina developer intervention ke automatically wapas up ho jata hai."}}]};export{e as default};
